---
// DRAFT — have a solicitor review before launch.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SELLER, LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED } from '../data/shop.js';
---
<Base
  title="Refund Policy | gazza.ltd"
  description="Refunds for the Making Tax Digital (MTD) Income Tax Readiness Tracker and the Winter Arc 90-Day Habit Tracker: your legal rights, instant download and the 14-day right to cancel, and our 14-day goodwill refund."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ name: 'Refund Policy' }]} />

    <h1>Refund Policy</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">Last updated {LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED}.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This policy covers both products sold on gazza.ltd: the Making Tax Digital (MTD)
        Income Tax Readiness Tracker (<strong>the workbook</strong>, an Excel file) and the
        Winter Arc 90-Day Habit Tracker (<strong>the tracker</strong>, a printable PDF).
        Each is a <strong>product</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your legal rights</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing in this policy affects your legal rights. Under the Consumer Rights Act
        2015, digital content must be of satisfactory quality, fit for purpose and as
        described. If the product you receive is faulty or not as described:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>you're entitled to a <strong>repair or replacement</strong>, for example a corrected file</li>
        <li>if we can't repair or replace it, or don't do so within a reasonable time and without significant inconvenience to you, you're entitled to a <strong>price reduction</strong>, which can be a <strong>full refund</strong></li>
        <li>if the product damages your device or other digital content because we didn't use reasonable care and skill, we'll <strong>repair the damage or compensate you</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We'll give any refund within 14 days of agreeing that you're entitled to it, to
        the payment method you used, and without charging you a fee. For more about your
        rights, contact <a href="https://www.citizensadvice.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Citizens Advice</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Instant download and the 14-day right to cancel</h2>
      <p>
        Online purchases usually come with a 14-day right to cancel. For digital
        downloads, that right ends once the download is made available, but only if
        you've asked for immediate access and confirmed that you understand you'll lose
        the right. This applies to both the workbook and the tracker (Consumer Contracts
        Regulations 2013). We ask you to do both at checkout by ticking the
        instant-download box on the product page. We record that consent (consent version
        ccr-2026-10-v1) with your Stripe payment record.
      </p>

      <h2>Our goodwill refund (14 days)</h2>
      <p>
        Even though the right to cancel ends once you download, we want you to be happy
        with your purchase. If a product isn't right for you, email us within
        <strong> 14 days of purchase</strong> and we'll normally refund you in full. You
        don't have to give a reason.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email <a href={`mailto:${SELLER.email}`}>{SELLER.email}</a> with your order reference, or the email address you used to buy.</li>
        <li>Please delete any copies of the product, and don't use any printed copies, once you've been refunded.</li>
        <li>This goodwill refund is at our discretion. We may refuse it where we reasonably think it's being misused, for example repeated purchase-and-refund. This <strong>doesn't</strong> limit your legal rights above, which apply whatever this section says.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How refunds are paid</h2>
      <p>
        Payments are processed by Stripe, so refunds go back through Stripe to your
        original payment method. They can take 5–10 working days to show on your statement.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {SELLER.name}, {SELLER.registeredOffice}. Email:
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${SELLER.email}`}>{SELLER.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
